71
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:33,860
A tuple is very similar to a list, but once it's created, it cannot be modified.

72
00:05:34,254 --> 00:05:42,212
For instance, if you write comma-separated values inside parentheses, you've created a tuple with two values and they stay exactly the same.

73
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:46,960
What this means is if you try to change a particular value, Python will raise an error.

74
00:05:47,214 --> 00:05:52,868
Tuples are great for storing data that shouldn't change, like a fixed location, phone numbers, or dimensions.

75
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,980
