81
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:37,220
Loops help us repeat a task multiple times without having to write the same line of code again and again.

82
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:41,892
In Python, we mainly use two types of loops, the for loop and the while loop.

83
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:46,852
A for loop is useful when you know exactly how many times you want to repeat something.

84
00:06:47,278 --> 00:06:54,948
For example, if you want to add up the numbers from 1 to 10, you could either do it manually or you could let Python handle it using a for loop.

85
00:06:55,310 --> 00:07:00,644
Here the loop goes through each number from 1 to 10 and keeps adding it to the variable called sum.

86
00:07:01,294 --> 00:07:07,652
On the other hand, a while loop is used when you want to keep repeating something until a certain condition is no longer true.

87
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,564
Let's say you want to add numbers only up to 5.

88
00:07:10,926 --> 00:07:15,812
You can use a while loop that starts at 1 and stops when the number becomes greater than 5.

89
00:07:16,238 --> 00:07:20,080
This allows you to automate repetitive tasks easily and efficiently.

