03:22:58,990 --> 03:23:05,232
Or in other words, horsepower is the dependent variable and miles per gallon is the independent variable.

2692
03:23:05,582 --> 03:23:08,804
So we see that our output variable is a continuous numerical.

2693
03:23:09,006 --> 03:23:14,884
And here we are trying to determine how does the horsepower of the car vary with its MPG.

2694
03:23:15,182 --> 03:23:17,540
So this is the concept of regression.

2695
03:23:18,414 --> 03:23:21,312
Now let's see some of the use cases of supervised learning.

2696
03:23:21,486 --> 03:23:23,716
So first we have spam classifier.

2697
03:23:24,046 --> 03:23:27,952
So how do you think your mail is being classified as whether it is spam or not?

2698
03:23:28,206 --> 03:23:32,272
So this spam detection basically works on the concept of filters.

2699
03:23:32,590 --> 03:23:37,232
So mainly there are two types of filters text filter and client filter.

2700
03:23:37,550 --> 03:23:44,964
The text filter works by using algorithm that detects which words and phrases are often used in the spam email.

2701
03:23:45,294 --> 03:23:53,252
So phrases like lottery or you won or free Bitcoin are often an immediate flag for removal by filters.

2702
03:23:53,710 --> 03:23:55,556
So next is the client filter.

2703
03:23:55,886 --> 03:24:03,652
As the name states, client filter understands the client identity and history to block malicious and annoying spam email.

2704
03:24:03,982 --> 03:24:05,860
So how does this client filter work?

2705
03:24:06,126 --> 03:24:10,912
Well, this is done by looking at all the messages of a certain user which he has sent out.

2706
03:24:11,182 --> 03:24:22,148
So if a user has sent out huge amount of emails constantly or several of the user's messages have already been marked as spam, then in that case their email will be blocked entirely.

2707
03:24:22,542 --> 03:24:24,592
So this brings us the use of blacklist.

2708
03:24:24,686 --> 03:24:27,952
So spam filters also include something known as blacklist.

2709
03:24:28,206 --> 03:24:33,380
So blacklisting is the process of adding known email addresses of a spammer to a list.

2710
03:24:33,632 --> 03:24:38,404
And this list prevents the user's messages to be forwarded to someone else.

2711
03:24:39,086 --> 03:24:42,656
Now let's look at the next use case fingerprint analysis.

2712
03:24:42,958 --> 03:24:47,588
So in fingerprint analysis, you save your fingerprint in a machine as a record.

2713
03:24:47,854 --> 03:24:53,348
So the machine checks the data and verifies whether the data belongs to you or not.

2714
03:24:53,710 --> 03:25:01,856
So once the data is saved into the machine, from next time, whenever you put your fingerprint on the machine, the machine will scan through all of its user data.

2715
03:25:02,126 --> 03:25:08,228
And if the machine finds a match of your fingerprint in its data, then your fingerprint will be verified.

2716
03:25:08,846 --> 03:25:15,428
Now that we've completed the different types of supervised learning algorithms, let's go ahead and understand what is unsupervised learning.

2717
03:25:15,790 --> 03:25:22,148
So when it comes to unsupervised learning, the input data doesn't have any labels associated with it.

2718
03:25:22,478 --> 03:25:31,136
The machine understands the underlying structure of the data to identify similar patterns and the data which is similar in nature is grouped together.

2719
03:25:31,342 --> 03:25:39,616
So here, even though there are no labels, the machine understands that all the apples are similar in nature and thus they are grouped together.

2720
03:25:39,854 --> 03:25:42,896
And same is the case with bananas and oranges.

2721
03:25:43,150 --> 03:25:46,148
So this is the concept of unsupervised learning.

2722
03:25:46,766 --> 03:25:50,756
Now let's go through an unsupervised machine learning algorithm called as k-means.

2723
03:25:51,056 --> 03:25:55,456
So the aim of k-means is to group similar data points into a single cluster.

2724
03:25:55,726 --> 03:26:00,804
So there must be high intra-cluster similarity and low intercluster similarity.

2725
03:26:01,166 --> 03:26:11,748
That is, all the data points within a cluster should be as similar as possible and all the data points between two different clusters should be as dissimilar as possible.

2726
03:26:12,174 --> 03:26:18,436
Or in other words, all the points inside cluster A should be very similar to each other.

2727
03:26:18,702 --> 03:26:24,932
But when we compare a point from cluster B with a point from cluster C, then they would be very dissimilar to each other.

2728
03:26:25,358 --> 03:26:29,412
And in K means clustering, K denotes the number of clusters to be formed.

2729
03:26:29,742 --> 03:26:34,692
So in this picture over here, the value of K is 3 and hence 3 clusters are formed.

2730
03:26:35,310 --> 03:26:37,892
Now let's go through a use case of unsupervised learning.

2731
03:26:38,414 --> 03:26:42,948
So Netflix recommendation is a perfect use case of unsupervised learning.

2732
03:26:43,406 --> 03:26:49,796
So more than 80% of the TV shows that you watch on Netflix are discovered through the platform's recommendation system.

2733
03:26:50,190 --> 03:26:57,700
It means the majority of what you watch on Netflix is the result of decisions made by a mysterious black box of an algorithm.

2734
03:26:58,190 --> 03:27:00,336
