2738
03:27:23,438 --> 03:27:25,536
And finally, there's reinforcement learning.

2739
03:27:25,902 --> 03:27:31,056
So in reinforcement learning, the algorithm learns through a system of rewards and punishment.

2740
03:27:31,374 --> 03:27:34,276
And the goal here is to maximize the total reward.

2741
03:27:34,638 --> 03:27:37,668
Let's take this example to understand reinforcement learning.

2742
03:27:38,158 --> 03:27:44,196
So here we have a self-driving car which is supposed to reach its destination without hitting any barricades.

2743
03:27:44,654 --> 03:27:49,764
So here, the self-driving car is the agent and the road is the environment.

2744
03:27:50,254 --> 03:27:53,124
Here the car takes an action and goes straight.

2745
03:27:53,454 --> 03:27:56,772
But when it goes straight, it directly hits the barricade.

2746
03:27:57,006 --> 03:28:00,676
Now since the car has taken a wrong action, it will be punished.

2747
03:28:01,070 --> 03:28:06,016
So the car realizes that going straight is wrong and it has to go right.

2748
03:28:06,318 --> 03:28:08,896
So when it goes right, it will be given a reward.

2749
03:28:09,134 --> 03:28:15,296
So this process continues and the car learns how to drive by itself without hitting any barricades.

2750
03:28:15,662 --> 03:28:20,132
So the obvious application of reinforcement learning is a self-driving car.

2751
03:28:20,366 --> 03:28:25,956
A recent study has shown that over 90% of road accidents are caused by human error.

2752
03:28:26,382 --> 03:28:27,856
