09:32:41,952 --> 09:32:47,684
Basically, what we're trying to understand here is what does the term knife stand for in this knife bias theorem?

8299
09:32:48,272 --> 09:32:57,552
So the word knife in knife bias basically refers to the assumption that all the features in a data set are independent of each other.

8300
09:32:58,272 --> 09:33:04,752
But if you consider real life scenarios or real life data sets, this assumption does not really apply.

8301
09:33:05,232 --> 09:33:05,472
Why?

8302
09:33:05,632 --> 09:33:08,912
Because, say, for example, you have a house price prediction data set.

8303
09:33:11,662 --> 09:33:18,244
You will have feature columns like number of bedrooms, number of bathrooms, balcony, or the area of the house, and so on.

8304
09:33:18,894 --> 09:33:26,756
Now, in real life, if you consider the area and number of bedrooms, number of bathrooms, so are supposed to have some sort of correlation between each other.

8305
09:33:26,990 --> 09:33:35,588
But what naive bias theorem does is it is going to consider that these features are independent of each other, that is, they have zero correlation between each other.

8306
09:33:36,078 --> 09:33:44,676
Now, this assumption will not apply in real life, but surprisingly, it works really well in many situations, especially for classification problems.

8307
09:33:45,056 --> 09:33:45,376
Right?

