09:38:18,894 --> 09:38:29,088
But if my model is failing to do the one goal it was trained for and it is giving me 98% accuracy, I can say my model is practically useless, right?

8366
09:38:29,550 --> 09:38:38,928
So this is why we need to handle the imbalance data sets using techniques like under-sampling, oversampling, and lastly we have SMOT, right?

8367
09:38:39,008 --> 09:38:47,808
So in under-sampling, basically we take random samples from our majority class till they are equal in size with our minority class, right?

8368
09:38:47,888 --> 09:38:50,404
So basically, we are making our data smaller.

8369
09:38:50,830 --> 09:39:01,888
