8370
09:39:01,968 --> 09:39:21,924
We are randomly going to pick 100 samples from our majority class, whereas in oversampling, if we have 1000 in our majority class and 100 in our minority class, we are going to keep duplicating these samples in our minority class until and unless they are equivalent to the size of our majority class.

8371
09:39:22,128 --> 09:39:32,608
That is, initially we had 1100 samples, now we are going to have 2000 samples in our entire data set, right?

8372
09:39:32,848 --> 09:39:35,808
So this is how under-sampling and oversampling works.

8373
09:39:35,968 --> 09:39:41,408
