Now, a typical example of a data set containing values from 1 to 10,000, basically a data set containing outliers would be say we are analyzing the salaries of various groups of people.

8865
10:16:35,630 --> 10:16:36,096
Alright.

8866
10:16:36,256 --> 10:16:45,316
Now there would be people who would be earning in thousands, somebody would be earning in lakhs, and there would be a very few people who would be earning in crores as well.

8867
10:16:45,966 --> 10:16:46,336
Alright.

8868
10:16:46,638 --> 10:16:50,756
So now the people who would be earning in crores would barely be either four or five.

8869
10:16:51,150 --> 10:16:51,616
Right?

8870
10:16:51,856 --> 10:16:54,884
These people are basically the outliers in our data set.

8871
10:16:55,216 --> 10:17:03,300
Now before we go ahead and train our model, we need to take care of these outliers or these values that range widely.

8872
10:17:03,776 --> 10:17:04,096
Right?

8873
10:17:04,590 --> 10:17:11,204
So some of the techniques that can be used in scenarios like this would be normalization or standardization.

8874
10:17:21,774 --> 10:17:33,856
So again, I have a separate video covering these topics of normalization and standardization, their implementation, the theoretical aspects, when to use which particular concept in complete detail.

8875
