Alright.

8877
10:17:36,718 --> 10:17:46,416
So normalization basically use methods like min max scaling, which helps to bring the values between 0 and 1.

8878
10:17:46,736 --> 10:17:47,296
Alright.

8879
10:17:47,536 --> 10:17:53,668
Whereas standardization uses mean of 0 and standard deviation of 1.

8880
10:17:54,190 --> 10:17:54,628
Alright.

8881
10:17:54,816 --> 10:17:58,896
So this basically helps models perform more efficiently, right?

8882
10:17:59,136 --> 10:18:02,084
So again, you need to choose your right scaling technique.

8883
10:18:02,318 --> 10:18:06,020
So if your data has outliers, normalization is going to work better.

8884
10:18:06,286 --> 10:18:10,256
But if your data does not have outliers, you need to perform standardization.

8885
